@page "/"

<PageTitle>Linkedin Post Sharing From Web Apps in 2 ways</PageTitle>

<h1>Linkedin Post Sharing From Web Apps in 2 ways</h1>
<p>Here using AspNet Core C# and Blazor</p>
<h3>1.Share-offsite</h3>
<ul>
	<li style="color:green">Works For Direct simple contents like Text,Urls...Just alike Simple Share button</li>
	<li style="color:green">Very Minimal code... i.e Just one line</li>
	<li style="color:red">Minimal features and No Direct media posting option at all</li>
	<li>If multiple URLs found then first link preview will be overridden on all. </li>
	<li style="color:purple">Previews will be changing over time wrt CRAWLers,so can be advantage/drawback both</li>
	<li style="color:blue">can view preview on 
		<a href="https://www.linkedin.com/post-inspector/" target="_blank">
			https://www.linkedin.com/post-inspector
		</a></li>
	<li>
		Code Example <code style="color:darkgreen">
		<a href="https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?text=am sharing my test text&url=SmartTown.in" target="_blank">
				<code>https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?text=am sharing my test text&url=SmartTown.in</code>
			</a>
		</code>
	</li>
</ul>
@* <hr /> *@
<h3>2.Share Using linkedin API</h3>
<p>For complete feature of linkedin internal platform features with lots of advanced. </p>
<ul>
	<li style="color:green">complete feature of linkedin internal platform features with lots of advanced.</li>
	<li style="color:darkmagenta">Requires linkedin developer app account registration(https://www.linkedin.com/developers/apps) and scopes (w_member_social,r_basicprofile with additional approvals)</li>
	<li style="color:red">Requires more technical knowledge for integration</li>
	<li>PLEASE MAKE SURE of proper clientid and secret set on appsettings.json</li>
	<li><a href="/share"> Click here to test Sharing Over Linkedin API</a></li>
</ul>
